MeanVC2: Robust Low-Latency Streaming Zero-Shot Voice Conversion
Guobin Ma, Yuxuan Xia, Yuepeng Jiang, Dake Guo, Hanke Xie, Jingbin Hu,
Yanbo Wang, Lei Xie, Pengcheng Zhu (ASLP@NPU and collaborators)
  Code:    https://github.com/ASLP-lab/MeanVC2
           (commit 13acf84c1bf135ea5edad9c245b345289b06b33e; the README
           states Apache-2.0, the repository has no LICENSE file)
  Weights: https://huggingface.co/ASLP-lab/MeanVC2
           (revision 39cdd19522fe896c227da691314d9a0e3b995486,
           license: apache-2.0)

From that Hugging Face repository:
  - meanvc2_120ms_40ms.safetensors -> dit.onnx, dit.int8.onnx, gtm.onnx
  - fastu2pp_160ms.pt (Fast-U2++ streaming ASR encoder, WeNet architecture)
                                    -> asr.onnx, asr.int8.onnx
    Only the embedding and the first 6 of the 12 encoder layers that the
    streaming path uses are in the graph.
  - vocos.pt (Vocos vocoder, 16 kHz) -> vocos.onnx, vocos.int8.onnx
    The inverse STFT is rewritten as matrix products and a transposed
    convolution.

fbank.onnx computes the Kaldi-compatible log-mel features that upstream gets
from torchaudio.compliance.kaldi.fbank (the mel filter bank values come from
torchaudio, BSD-2-Clause, https://github.com/pytorch/audio).

